thin (2u + 1.25e-08) of T): |r - ref| < 2.04e-07 |T| < 3.42 ulp\n        not bit-exact: c = 0.02516423: original 0.07598506, rewrite 0.07598505 (1 ulp apart)\n        bound against the reference: 3 ulp\n        (line 1: vec3 Gamma(vec3 c) { return pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)); })\n  done already by spirv-opt -O (the GLSL divides, the module multiplies):\n    %48 = OpFMul %v3float %46 %53   (spirv-opt -O: x / 1.055 as x * 0.94786733)\n        k = fl(1/1.055) = 0.94786733; k*d = 1 + delta with delta = -1.25e-08 (k*d is exact in double)\n          x*k = (x/d)(1 + delta), so |fl(x*k) - x/d| <= ulp/2 + |x/d| |delta| < (0.5 + 2^24 |delta|) ulp = 0.709 ulp (|v| < 2^24 ulp(v); subnormal results alike)\n          x/d correctly rounded is within 0.5 ulp, and both are floats: they differ by at most 1 ulp\n          Vulkan OpFDiv: 2.5 ulp (for |y| in [2^-126, 2^126]); the multiply is correctly rounded: 0.709 <= 2.5, so it is within the precision the division already had\n        not bit-exact: c + 0.055 = 0.52750045: / 1.055 gives 0.5000005, * 0.94786733 gives 0.5000004 (the quotient within |delta| of a rounding midpoint)\n        (line 1: vec3 Gamma(vec3 c) { return pow((c + 0.055) / 1.055, vec3(2.4)); })\n  approximations (cheaper, not applied: say `approx ulp N` to allow one):\n    pow ~ degree-2 minimax polynomial, cost 3 (-5): relative error < 0.133 (2.53526e+06 ulp), beyond the original's precision\n      the sink refuses it: it would move the stored value by up to 0.133, more than the 0.00392 a step of the sink allows\n    pow ~ degree-3 minimax polynomial, cost 4 (-4): relative error < 0.0164 (279074 ulp), beyond the original's precision\n      the sink refuses it: it would move the stored value by up to 0.0164, more than the 0.00392 a step of the sink allows\n    pow ~ degree-4 minimax polynomial, cost 5 (-3): relative error < 0.00443 (74724 ulp), beyond the original's precision\n      the sink refuses it: it would move the stored value by up to 0.00444, more th